# Palette and diagnostics: run tests

When you edit `src/palette-layer.js`, `src/palette-diagnostics.js`, or `src/palette-layer.test.js`:

1. **Run unit tests** after changes: `npm test`
2. Fix any failing tests before considering the change done.

Unit tests cover `remapFrame` and `aspectFitRect`.

## Verifying in the browser (check your own work)

- **Agent browser:** If the dev server is running (`npm run dev`), you can open http://localhost:5173 in the browser tool: navigate, click (e.g. display toggle, Run diagnostics), and take screenshots to verify UI and flows. Prefer doing this after UI or flow changes so the agent checks its work instead of the user.
- **Runtime diagnostics (Step 0–3):** If the user has **Chrome DevTools MCP** (or ConsoleSpy) configured, you can ask to inspect the browser console for the tab running the app and read pass/fail from the diagnostics. See [docs/history/archive/cursor-web-testing.md](docs/history/archive/cursor-web-testing.md) (project root). If MCP is not set up, the user may paste diagnostic output; use it to decide fixes.
